# Wave W17-AD (Amber Sea — East): resort rock — a clean pale boulder standing in the shipped sea, its faces worked smooth and light, foam collar at its base (design: rock spikes in pink shell sand at the Reefside end — the lane’s rocks are the harbour’s kept stones). East’s own rock — split from North’s deep-shadow shrine rock by light entire (pale worked faces in bright water vs dark stone in the channel) and from Foamline’s footing rock by keeping: this stone is a harbour ornament, that one is a walkway footing.
